# Repository Structure

CrossExam AI is a monorepo. Place new code in the right top-level directory
rather than creating new top-level directories or mixing concerns:

```
crossexam-ai/
├── frontend/   # Next.js static-export app (client-side SPA only, no SSR/API routes)
├── backend/    # LangGraph agent (witness, opposing counsel, hearing officer, debrief nodes), deployed to AgentCore Runtime
├── rag/        # Corpus ingestion (statute, regs, case decisions) + local embedding pipeline (FAISS/Chroma)
├── infra/      # S3 / CloudFront / Lambda deployment config
└── docs/       # Architecture notes, case file schema, persona design
```

- Backend proxy/Lambda code (SigV4 signing, streaming passthrough to
  AgentCore) belongs in `infra/` or a dedicated proxy subfolder, not mixed
  into `frontend/`, since the browser must never hold AWS credentials.
- New persona logic (witness / opposing counsel / hearing officer / debrief)
  belongs in `backend/` as distinct LangGraph nodes — do not collapse
  personas into a single prompt/role.
- New corpus sources or embedding logic belong in `rag/`.
- Architecture/design decisions and schema definitions (e.g. the per-session
  case file schema) belong in `docs/`, and significant architectural changes
  should also be reflected in `ARCHITECTURE.md` at the repo root.
